WEBVTT

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.310
Final Exams!

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:17.070
Okay, everyone,

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.740
pencils down, please.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.200
Second semester finals are now over,

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.630
but try not to slack off too much over break.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.740
With that, everyone,

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:32.260
be careful not to catch any colds over break.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:34.140
Okay!

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:40.390
All right!

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:45.600
So for announcements, we have the 
faculty's notice about counseling

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:49.720
and the student council's solicitation for 
donations to the year-end charity event.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:52.930
And the new segment we started last week

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:55.150
has gotten all of this good feedback.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:56.910
I guess

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:01.830
people want to hear heartwarming 
stories when it gets cold out.

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:04.020
Yeah...

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.840
I think I can understand that.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:13.770
What should I do?

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:18.410
I'm really up against a fall.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:23.930
<b>Goodbye à la Mode</b>

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.840
<i>Did you all do well on your finals?</i>

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.890
<i>Try not to get sick now that the stress is off.</i>

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:27.790
<i>Well, that's all for today.</i>

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:30.050
<i>See you, bye-bye!</i>

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:31.760
See you...

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:35.610
Chloe-san, what's wrong?

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:37.560
Yulia-san...

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:41.710
Did you not do well on your tests?

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:42.790
My tests?

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:44.480
No...

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.500
I'm not worried about the tests.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:48.620
I know!

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.250
You're worried about Christmas, right?

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:52.280
Christmas?

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:56.510
It's hard to choose Christmas presents, isn't it?

00:01:56.510 --> 00:02:00.760
Or maybe you can't decide what 
to wear for the Christmas party?

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:04.190
It'll be our first Christmas at Seiou.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.460
I'm so excited!

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:09.140
Chloe-san?

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.820
What were you talking about?

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:16.070
Christmas.

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:17.280
Oh, yeah,

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:20.000
it's Christmas...

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:24.830
Chloe-san?

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:29.250
Huh?

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.000
Hey, Akiho-oneechan.

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:36.530
I heard it's good to eat 
pumpkin during winter.

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:37.010
But...

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.840
What does winter have to do with pumpkins?

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.010
Oh, apparently,

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:47.020
pumpkins help make up the nutrients
your body tends to lack during winter.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:48.690
That's why people in the past

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:53.340
associated pumpkins with winter, 
and decided to eat them then.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.110
But why bring that up, Mei?

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:01.190
Chloe-san asked me yesterday,
but I didn't know the answer.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:04.990
Also, she wanted to know what 
the ceremonial hamaya were for...

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:10.410
You're the daughter of a priest.
You should know that.

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:14.680
I mean, I have a general idea, but...

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:16.230
Oh, Chloe-san.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.420
I found out the answer to your pumpkin question.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:23.890
Chloe-san?

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:32.960
Kokomi-chan.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:34.310
Mochizuki-senpai.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.000
Hey!

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.190
So, did you think about what I asked you?

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:43.730
I already said I didn't want to do it.

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:46.140
Huh, really?

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.320
You haven't changed your mind?

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.570
No, I never will!

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:50.870
Huh?

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:52.500
What are you talking about?

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:54.040
Nude—

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:57.790
What?

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:00.420
Oh, Chloe-san.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.430
Was that really Chloe-san?

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:13.440
I thought it was...

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.690
She looks down.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:23.150
I wonder if she's worried about something.

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:26.810
What's wrong, Chloe-san?

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:29.930
N-Nothing is wrong.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:31.240
But...

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:33.580
I told you, nothing's wrong.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:38.920
Murakami-senpai.

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:41.920
Shiina-san.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.470
Did Chloe-san tell you anything?

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:46.080
No...

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:49.220
It was more like she was trying 
to avoid talking to me.

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:50.970
I knew it.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:53.000
You knew what?

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:58.000
Everyone's saying Chloe-san
has been acting strangely.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:58.990
Yeah...

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:01.160
That's worrying...

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:02.360
Oh, I know.

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:05.360
How about asking Sakurai-san?

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:11.430
Oh, there you are, Chloe-senpai.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.580
Akane-san...

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:14.790
Tomo-san...

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:18.470
We came to interview you today.

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:19.620
Interview?

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:20.250
Yeah!

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:21.750
And we're on.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:25.050
It's a new segment we started last month.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:28.000
We have everyone talk freely on the subject of

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.720
words that left an impression on them.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:34.980
Chloe-senpai, what words have 
left an impression on you?

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:38.980
It can be something happy, serious, anything...

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:40.690
Uh...

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:45.650
It can even be something 
you're worried about lately.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:49.660
Are you worried about something right now?

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.270
Worried...

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:53.660
Please, tell us!

00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:58.370
I'm sorry.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:05:59.360
Huh?

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:05.650
I have nothing to talk about.

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:24.570
I'm sorry I wasn't able to help.

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.200
No, it's okay. Don't worry about it.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.740
Um, I'll try asking her.

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:32.410
You will?

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:35.580
My way might be a little forceful,

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:38.040
but I think I can get it out of her.

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:40.030
Forceful?

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:40.860
Yes.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:44.570
Mochizuki-senpai, could you help me out a bit?

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:44.920
Huh?

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:47.170
Me?

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.650
What's going on, Erena-san?

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:54.360
I don't feel like hanging out today.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:59.960
Just come along. There's someone 
who wants to talk to you, just for a bit.

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:02.060
Huh?

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:04.440
Kokomi-san?

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:06.940
What's wrong?

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:10.520
Why did you have me come here?

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:13.380
Chloe-san, do you remember?

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:16.160
I found the picture you dropped here.

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:18.450
Oui.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:23.210
You said you'd do something
for me in return, right?

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:27.050
I'll do whatever you want, Kokomi.

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:32.800
I told you I'd think about it, right?

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:34.070
Oui.

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:36.470
Well then, here's what I'd like to ask...

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:39.850
Will you tell me what's worrying you?

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:44.730
I-I'm not worried about anything.

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:49.950
In Japan, if you lie, an ogre 
will pull out your tongue.

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:54.670
Non! I don't want that!

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:56.780
Please tell me the truth, then.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:10.510
The truth is, my family told 
me to come back home.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.560
Huh? For New Year's?

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:16.350
That's not really something
to be so worried about...

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:21.350
Non, they want me to leave Seiou,

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:24.850
and never come back to Japan!

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:25.850
What?!

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:26.860
What?!

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:30.020
Huh?

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:35.260
I told them I didn't want to go, of course.

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:38.620
That I couldn't bear leaving.

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:40.290
But...

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:45.120
My family won't let me stay here.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:46.940
Why not?

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:48.040
That's terrible.

00:08:48.580 --> 00:08:52.870
They said it's too dangerous to 
let me live alone in Japan.

00:08:52.870 --> 00:08:57.660
But you came here when 
you were in your first year.

00:08:57.660 --> 00:09:01.010
I don't know why they decided 
to do this now, either.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:05.520
Don't look so sad, everyone.

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:09.830
I didn't say anything because 
I didn't want to upset you.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:12.530
But I made you all sad, after all.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:20.030
Is it possible to convince your 
parents to change their minds?

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:21.030
Huh?

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:25.010
If they say it's dangerous for 
Chloe-san to live here by herself,

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:27.040
then we just need to show them it's safe.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:29.840
In other words,

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:36.100
we convince them that Seiou 
Academy is a wonderful place.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:39.430
I've got it!

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:42.080
Let's have the film research club help us.

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:43.860
Okay,

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:45.270
we're ready to roll.

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:47.730
<b>Yuzuki

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:54.070
I'd like to introduce you to Seiou Academy.

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:55.780
Students in our academy

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:59.070
take part in a variety of athletic clubs

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:02.840
including golf and billiards,

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:07.830
as well as many fine arts clubs, like music and art.

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:11.240
Seiou has both literary and
physical education programs,

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:13.590
including several sports programs.

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:18.720
Our excellent facilities and equipment provide 
a perfect environment for practicing.

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:22.500
Japan also has a very proud cultural heritage...

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:24.720
As well as many things to see.

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:41.070
We teachers prioritize student safety
and student livelihood above all else.

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:44.370
We stay in contact with our students' guardians,

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:47.080
maintaining relationships of mutual trust.

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:52.880
Okay, cut!

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:59.220
Murakami-senpai!

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:00.970
Yes?

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:05.000
Please teach us how to
write a letter in French!

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:07.930
Um, why are you all here together?

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:09.020
<b>Kitties 5</b>

00:11:10.090 --> 00:11:11.480
We are

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:13.720
members of Kitties 5!

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:14.770
Right...

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:17.440
We heard about Chloe-san!

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:20.780
Chloe-san comes to visit Erika a lot.

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:23.660
That's why we want to help Chloe-san!

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:27.660
But we don't know any French 
other than "oui" and "non"!

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:34.500
We might be able to write something 
simple if we use a dictionary.

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:36.610
We'll do it!

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:48.940
This might be one of the best movies that
the film research club has ever put together.

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:51.060
We all worked hard on it.

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:53.810
Everyone...

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:57.610
Merci!

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:03.320
Maybe they'll change their 
minds when they see this.

00:12:15.490 --> 00:12:16.680
Chloe-san?

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:25.260
Um...

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:27.760
It didn't work.

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:32.370
Huh?

00:12:34.150 --> 00:12:38.950
Why can't Chloe-san's family understand?

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:40.860
I know how you all feel,

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:44.630
but I also understand how
it feels to be a parent.

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:45.280
Huh?

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:49.740
They're not telling her to 
come home just to be mean.

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:53.130
Parents worry about their 
children because they love them.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:54.750
But...

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:56.750
There might be

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:59.400
something going on with their family, as well.

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:01.680
You mustn't blame them.

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:06.870
Besides, I'm sure Chloe-san is the one who 
wishes she didn't have to go most of all.

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:11.870
Instead of trying to force her to stay

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:14.220
and making her feel even worse,

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:17.980
it might be better for you all to 
just give her a nice send-off.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:25.200
So, it might be better if we tell her

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:26.910
that we can see each other again,

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:30.410
instead of telling her to stay.

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:33.160
That's true.

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:36.160
Nowadays, we can talk on the internet, too.

00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:39.480
We'll only be apart for a little while.

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:41.060
You're right.

00:13:41.060 --> 00:13:45.550
We can always go visit her in France, too.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:47.030
Hey, I know!

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:50.180
Why don't we throw a farewell 
party for Chloe-san?

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:52.560
It's also Christmas, anyway.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:53.930
We can do it at my café.

00:13:54.470 --> 00:13:56.520
I'll take care of the entertainment!

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:58.920
I'll help with the shopping.

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:01.410
I can totally help carry stuff.

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:04.020
You'll all want to dress up, right?

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:05.650
Leave the hair and makeup to me!

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:09.720
I might be able to borrow 
a santa outfit from my work.

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:12.630
Oh, the arts and crafts club can help, too.

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:14.720
Let's make this a great party.

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:16.200
For Chloe-san.

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:17.450
All right.

00:14:17.450 --> 00:14:19.710
Let's start getting ready!

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:21.460
Yeah!

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:21.730
Chloe-san's going home? I'll miss her...

00:14:21.730 --> 00:14:23.230
Chloe-san's going home? I'll miss her...

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:24.730
Everybody! We're having a farewell and 
Christmas party at Sasahara-senpai's cafe 
for Chloe-senpai on Christmas Eve, starting 
at 5:30 P.M. Everyone should come. 

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:25.230
Really?!

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:25.730
Really?!

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:26.070
Got it. I'll be there!

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:26.360
I wouldn't miss it.

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:26.740
I'll be there with our club president.

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:27.490
Is there anything I can do? I want to help.

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:27.990
I can help with cooking, if anyone needs it.

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:28.490
Let's get some good food together for Chloe-san.

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:29.070
You plan to have cake, right? I'll bring a Stollen cake.

00:14:29.070 --> 00:14:29.450
I'll try to come up with something I can help with, too.

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:30.360
I'll definitely be there!

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:31.320
Of course I'll come!

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:32.930
So she's definitely leaving? That's so sad...

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.730
Okay, see you tomorrow.

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:06.760
Look forward to hearing our new song.

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:09.090
Be careful on your way home.

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:10.920
We will!

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:15.100
We should be going home, too.

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:19.100
Yeah, we've finished the 
preparations for all the food,

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:21.060
and we're all done decorating.

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:24.200
Now we just wait for—

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:25.320
Hi there.

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:28.550
I brought it.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:33.570
Oh, très bien!

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:35.750
Chloe-senpai.

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:37.120
It wasn't cold out?

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:39.840
That's a beautiful tree.

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:41.080
Also,

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:43.830
it smells like butter in here.

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:45.630
It's such a pleasant smell.

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:51.000
We're going to bake croquembouche, 
panettone, and galette.

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:53.640
I guess I get to be the taste-tester.

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:55.640
You're so silly, Mochizuki-san.

00:15:57.330 --> 00:16:01.070
Other countries have so many 
different kinds of sweets.

00:16:01.070 --> 00:16:04.240
I guess Japan has ohagi.

00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:07.020
I didn't like ohagi at first.

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:09.320
I couldn't get over the beans being sweet,

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:11.680
but I like them now.

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:16.490
Papa?

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:18.930
Hello,

00:16:19.140 --> 00:16:20.100
Papa?

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:21.450
What's the matter?

00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:24.350
I'm with my friends right now.

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:25.690
What?!

00:16:25.690 --> 00:16:27.440
You're coming here?

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:28.860
Really?

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:30.340
Okay...

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:34.800
What's wrong?

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:38.970
My papa's coming here.

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:40.720
What?!

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:42.920
No way. Why?

00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:45.680
Is he going to take you back home?!

00:16:45.680 --> 00:16:46.570
When?

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:48.690
He's not going to take you
back right away, right?

00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:52.030
We want to have the party tomorrow for you.

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:54.700
What should we do?

00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:59.590
Everyone, calm down.

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:01.960
Yeah, calm down.

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:03.540
We should talk to him first.

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:06.290
Y-You're right.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.440
Even if it's awkward,

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:12.260
Chloe-san's dad will be a valued guest.

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:14.550
We should welcome him with all our hearts.

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:17.300
You always know what to do, Sasahara-senpai!

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:22.120
Hey, let's get him something 
special to drink to welcome him.

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:24.490
What should we do?

00:17:24.490 --> 00:17:25.980
Do we have something?

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:29.310
Sasahara-senpai, could you stand near the door?

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:32.570
If you could greet him first...

00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:37.360
Papa!

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:42.560
My sweet little girl.

00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:44.350
Let me see you.

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:46.580
You look like you've been well.

00:17:49.530 --> 00:17:51.030
Let me introduce you.

00:17:51.030 --> 00:17:53.290
This is my father.

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:57.090
I appreciate you all taking care of Chloe.

00:17:57.600 --> 00:18:01.850
Thank you for your letter and movie, as well.

00:18:02.170 --> 00:18:05.350
Chloe has such good friends.

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:09.730
Um, why does Chloe-senpai have to go home?

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:11.860
S-Sakurai-san...

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:15.360
We want to stay with Chloe-chan!

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:17.030
Please let her stay!

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:28.970
Everyone, thank you for
caring so much for Chloe.

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:31.130
But as her father,

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:36.160
I'm worried about Chloe living on her own.

00:18:38.110 --> 00:18:40.640
With all due respect, she has us.

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:43.640
She won't be alone.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:45.710
Kokomi-chan is right.

00:18:45.710 --> 00:18:49.480
What is it that makes you worry?

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:53.280
Seiou Academy is a safe place, 
and a great environment.

00:18:53.280 --> 00:18:56.440
I'm a transfer student, 
as well, but I'm safe here.

00:18:57.110 --> 00:18:58.280
Being hit.

00:18:58.720 --> 00:18:59.570
Huh?

00:18:59.940 --> 00:19:03.300
I've never heard of corporal 
punishment at Seiou.

00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:05.040
108 times.

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:10.460
When New Year's comes, they start 
selling weapons on the street corners.

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:15.170
You have to eat things
that could kill you, too.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:20.470
Did you tell your dad that, Chloe-senpai?

00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:23.970
Oui, it's all true...

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:28.650
Wait, could you explain everything
to us from the beginning?

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:30.940
What does he mean about being hit?

00:19:31.550 --> 00:19:34.150
To eliminate wicked feelings...

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:36.880
Wait... 108 times?

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:39.900
You mean the Buddhist New Year's bells?

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:41.390
Huh?

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:42.640
Yes, that!

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:45.410
But <i>you're</i> not the one getting hit...

00:19:45.640 --> 00:19:47.580
What's the weapon thing about, then?

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:51.330
Magical arrows to keep evil away!

00:19:53.430 --> 00:19:55.290
You mean the hamaya?

00:19:56.080 --> 00:20:02.220
And you put rope and bamboo spears in 
front of your homes to keep demons out!

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:07.120
You mean shimenawa and kadomatsu,
the New Year's decorations, right?

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:09.520
Those aren't technically weapons...

00:20:09.940 --> 00:20:16.100
And there's this "mochi" thing 
that could kill you if you eat it!

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:20.830
They're so good that no one 
would ever refuse one.

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:25.970
Do you understand now?

00:20:25.970 --> 00:20:29.410
Of course her parents would
 be worried about her.

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:35.000
We understand.

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:40.670
May we clarify the information 
that Chloe-san has given you?

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:43.880
<b>Café Cosmos</b>

00:20:41.880 --> 00:20:43.880
How can this be?!

00:20:44.190 --> 00:20:47.350
Then, there's no danger?

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:48.650
That's right.

00:20:48.650 --> 00:20:53.800
For example, this is a fève,
a figurine that you put in a king cake.

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:55.630
Chloe lent it to me.

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:58.870
Just think of it as having Chloe

00:20:58.870 --> 00:21:01.160
eat one of those cakes with this in it.

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:02.760
I see.

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:06.760
So what she said was not wrong, 
but not exactly right.

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:09.990
Everyone, it seems I didn't 
fully understand the situation.

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:11.360
Papa?

00:21:11.880 --> 00:21:12.800
Chloe,

00:21:14.720 --> 00:21:19.210
it seems that you have not yet
fully grasped Japanese culture.

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:20.800
Oui...

00:21:21.230 --> 00:21:25.180
You should stay here longer and study.

00:21:25.180 --> 00:21:26.350
Papa...

00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:26.760
So...

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:31.390
Does that mean Chloe-san doesn't have to leave?

00:21:31.740 --> 00:21:36.200
Yes. In fact, I cannot take her away now.

00:21:36.200 --> 00:21:37.760
Yay!

00:21:37.760 --> 00:21:41.110
Papa... I can stay in Japan?!

00:21:42.540 --> 00:21:43.400
Oui.

00:21:45.080 --> 00:21:46.780
Papa!

00:21:56.910 --> 00:22:00.870
<b>Café Cosmos</b>

00:21:57.940 --> 00:22:00.880
Okay, everyone look forward 
to the party tomorrow.

00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:04.130
Remember, no being late.

00:22:05.230 --> 00:22:06.180
Of course.

00:22:06.180 --> 00:22:08.800
Everyone, make sure you dress up.

00:22:09.310 --> 00:22:10.600
Right!

00:22:09.310 --> 00:22:10.600
Oui!

00:22:20.550 --> 00:22:21.950
Sneg!

00:22:21.950 --> 00:22:23.320
It's snowing!

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:24.840
<b>Preview</b>

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:14.180
Kokomi-san, did you write your New Year's cards?

00:24:14.180 --> 00:24:17.360
Yes, I've finished them.

00:24:17.360 --> 00:24:18.900
Très bien!

00:24:18.900 --> 00:24:21.560
Everyone, the next episode is the last.

00:24:21.560 --> 00:24:22.890
One, two...

00:24:21.810 --> 00:24:24.840
<b>Episode 12: Girlfriend xxx</b>

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:24.350
Girlfriend!
